.TH SDL_FORCE_INLINE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_FORCE_INLINE \- A macro to demand a function be inlined.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_begin_code.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_FORCE_INLINE __forceinline
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a command to the compiler to inline a function\[char46] SDL uses this macro in its public headers for a handful of simple functions\[char46] On compilers without forceinline support, this is defined to
.BR "static SDL_INLINE" ,
which is often good enough\[char46]
.PP
This symbol is used in SDL\(aqs headers, but apps and other libraries are welcome to use it for their own interfaces as well\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

